 "new_string": "This task-specific note is based on correct recurring instances plus demonstrations; treat it as a strong prior, re-derive directions and eligible motifs from every fresh grid, and validate all dimensions and changed coordinates.\n\n### Further solved instance: select the supported ray, not every diagonal pair\nA 28x12 uniform-5 test had a 2 diagonal at `(25,8),(26,7),(27,6)` and a crossing/adjacent 0 diagonal at `(26,6),(27,7)`. Correct output extended the 2s toward NE (up-right) from the upper endpoint, adding `(24,9),(23,10),(22,11)` to the right edge; original cells remained unchanged. The 0 pair did not generate a ray. The first attempted output added a 0 ray up-left from that pair as well as the correct 2 ray and was rejected. Thus do not extend every pair/diagonal that happens to be present: identify the contextual intended motif/ray and leave incidental competing diagonal pairs unchanged. This instance's 2 cells made a length-3 uninterrupted diagonal, while the 0s were only a short 2-cell diagonal within the motif. The rightward ray terminates at the grid boundary; no cells are recolored or overwritten."
